      "story_id": 1,
      "headline": "Women's Reservation and Delimitation Bills fail in Lok Sabha; Modi addresses nation, blames opposition for 'female foeticide'",
      "summary": "India's government introduced a special parliamentary session (April 16\u201318) to pass three linked bills: the Constitution (131st Amendment) Bill for fresh delimitation, a seat expansion to 816\u2013850 MPs, and early implementation of 33% women's reservation in legislatures by 2029. The bills failed to secure the required two-thirds majority on April 17, with Congress, TMC, DMK and Samajwadi Party voting against. Modi delivered a nationally televised address on April 18 accusing the opposition of committing 'bhrun hatya' (female foeticide), while Congress president Kharge countered that Modi 'mentioned Congress 59 times and women barely at all.' Home Minister Shah piloted the bills in Lok Sabha, presented state-by-state seat projections to reassure southern states, and offered an oral guarantee of 50% seat increases that he later declined to formalise in writing. BJP and NDA allies announced nationwide protests; CPM and CPI filed complaints with the Election Commission alleging Modi's address violated the Model Code of Conduct during ongoing state elections.",
